A||N||5||mrfixit58||Junk Yard T-Top SCORE!!!||||10||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||01-17-2000||08:44 AM||||Sometimes you just get lucky. While cruzin my local U-Pull-It yard I noticed a Fiero that they just pulled in. IT was an 86 with a T-Top. I went back the next day with a 12” gas powered cut-off saw and removed the entire roof being careful to first remove the weather stripping. The whole set-up is there but some of the pieces are in rough shape. The worst are the corner pieces in which the locking pins slide. The other piece that rough is the weather stripping that is attached to the tops. Someone filled the gap with some kind of goop that may destroy the seals if I try to remove it. Now for a couple of questions:<P>Does GM or anyone offer any replacement parts for the T-Top cars, specifically the two items mentioned above?<P>Has anyone installed a T-Top kit? If so, how much of the body needs to be disassembled? If I decide to try this on my car, do you need to reinforce the body or top while you cut the side supports and before you install the middle brace?<P>Is there any place I can go on the Web that will show an exploded view of the T-Top installation?<P>Thanks again for your help<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000001||TOM||01-17-2000||10:27 AM||||I am going to be offering reproduction corner caps and light covers. I would install the center brace before cutting the side out.||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||01-17-2000||11:10 AM||||Congratulations on your find mrfixit! You really need to get in touch with Fiero Parts and Appraisals in Maine. Email is fieroparts@aol.com<BR>Last year they sent me a Price and Availability List, which includes T-Top Restoration Kits ($850), and prices for all trim caps, glass, seals, and moldings. They also sent me an exploded view of the T-Roof, even instructions on replacing the T-Top P-Seals! If you'd like me to run off some copies and mail them to you or anyone else, LMK, I'd be more than happy to help you out!  -joel||||reg||10
Z||000003||mrfixit58||01-17-2000||01:29 PM||||Tom... Great news. Please let me and the group know when you have the corner caps available.<P>Turbo... Pictures would be great... and worth at least 1000 words. Are the parts that they sell new? Do they off just pieces (like the window weather stripping)?<P>Thanks again for the info/advice. <P>Roy||||reg||14
Z||000004||turbo86se||01-18-2000||01:07 AM||||Roy, as far as I know, Fiero Parts and Appraisals bought out the remaining parts from Skylight (C&C). Everything they offer is brand-new. If you'd like a copy, LMK, it will be in the mail ASAP!<BR>Take care,   joel <BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfixit58||01-18-2000||02:03 PM||||That would be great. I'll E-mail you my snail mail. If anyone else has any useful tips on installing a T-top, please let me know. I plan on getting my car out of storage in a couple of weeks and start getting it road worthy. I am seriously thinking of adding the T-Top before I do the paint. <P>Thanks again for your help.<BR>Roy||||reg||14
